.TH GENETREE 1 2000-1月 "solver_opts" "solver_opts"
.SH NAME
solver_opts \- Override the fixed point solving options of a trained model at runtime, so that
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIsolver_opts(\fBtree\fR as <generic> XGBoostGRN, 
\fBiterations\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBdamping\fR as double = -1, 
\fBtolerance\fR as double = -1, 
\fBhard_cap\fR as integer = -1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Override the fixed point solving options of a trained model at runtime, so that
 the solver can be tuned without re-training the whole network.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBtree\fB \fR\- the trained [XGBoostGRN](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GeneTree.XGBoostGRN) model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBiterations\fB \fR\- 
 the soft iteration limit; a negative value keeps the current value.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdamping\fB \fR\- 
 the damping coefficient \fBalpha\fR in the range (0, 1]; a negative value keeps the
 current value. A larger alpha moves faster but is easier to oscillate.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtolerance\fB \fR\- 
 the relative convergence tolerance; a negative value keeps the current value.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBhard_cap\fB \fR\- 
 the hard iteration limit which is used when the soft limit is not enough for
 convergence; a negative value keeps the current value, \fB0\fR restores the default
 (\fBmax(iterations * 5, 300)\fR).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the input model object that the solver options have been applied.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the control steady state and the last perturbation result are invalidated, so the
 next perturbation experiment re-solves the control steady state with the new
 options.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneTree
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
